// Vitest Snapshot v1, https://vitest.dev/guide/snapshot.html

exports[`crimp process data (PRD §28, §30) > is deterministic: same HIR twice, byte-identical output 1`] = `
"ASSEMBLY INSTRUCTIONS — crimp-process rev A
Units: mm. Generated from HIR 0.1.0; every step references design object IDs.

Materials
---------
 1. Gather 2x CONN-2 — used by connector:M1, connector:M2.
 2. Gather 1x CONN-4 — used by connector:J1.

Cut wires
---------
 3. Cut W1: 18AWG red, 300 mm.
 4. Cut W2: 18AWG black, 300 mm.
 5. Cut W3: 20AWG yellow, 420 mm.
 6. Cut W4: 22AWG blue, 260 mm.

Crimp terminations
------------------
 7. Crimp 1 termination(s) with terminal GH-2210-9 on 20AWG wire: J1.3.
      Strip length not specified in the terminal record.
      Crimp tool CT-9082.
      Die not specified in the terminal record.
      Crimp height not specified in the terminal record; no window to measure against.
      Pull force not specified in the terminal record; no minimum to test against.
      Terminal data is unverified — confirm against the terminal datasheet before setting the press.
 8. Crimp 3 termination(s) with terminal GH-4471-3 (Grayhaven Contacts) on 18AWG wire: J1.1, J1.2, M1.1.
      Strip length 6.43 mm.
      Crimp tool CT-9082.
      Die D-7734.
      Crimp height 1.263 to 1.417 mm, measured with a micrometer across the crimp barrel.
      Pull force minimum 73.6 N, checked by tensile pull test.
 9. Crimp 1 termination(s) with terminal GH-4471-3 (Grayhaven Contacts) on 22AWG wire: M2.2.
      Strip length 6.43 mm.
      Crimp tool CT-9082.
      Die D-7734.
      Crimp height 1.263 to 1.417 mm, measured with a micrometer across the crimp barrel.
      Pull force minimum 73.6 N, checked by tensile pull test.

Populate connectors
-------------------
10. Populate J1 (CONN-4):
      cavity 1: W1
      cavity 2: W2
      cavity 3: W3
      cavity 4: W4
11. Populate M1 (CONN-2):
      cavity 1: W1
      cavity 2: W2
12. Populate M2 (CONN-2):
      cavity 1: W3
      cavity 2: W4

Inspection
----------
13. Verify every cavity against the pinout table; check seating/lock engagement.
14. Verify wire colors and labels against the schedule.
15. Verify branch lengths and sleeve coverage against the board drawing.

Test
----
16. Run the continuity-test procedure (tests.csv / test-plan.json); record results per test ID.
"
`;
